# Style through the theme system

Do not hard-code QSS strings or magic pixel sizes on widgets. Tag the widget and put look-and-layout tokens in `style/theme_light.qss`.

```cpp
// BAD
listWidget->setStyleSheet(QStringLiteral("QListWidget { background: transparent; }"));
dialog.setMinimumSize(960, 300);
item->setSizeHint(QSize(150, 52));

// GOOD
Style::setRole(listWidget, "chipStrip");
Style::setRole(&dialog, "fileOrder");
Style::setVariant(button, "ghost");
Style::setSize(button, "sm");
```

QSS owns colors, padding, radius, min/max width and height. Match existing zinc tokens (`#e4e4e7`, `#f4f4f5`, `#09090b`) instead of one-off palettes.

Widget-only Qt APIs (flow, wrapping, drag-drop, scrollbar policy) stay in C++. Pair horizontal `QListView` flow with wrapping and a vertical scrollbar so many items can scale.
